speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, the reply to this question is as follows:
1. (a) No information is as yet available on the amount of grain dried at fine elevators;
(b)	There are no government elevators at the head of the lakes;
(c)	This information is not available on a monthly basis. As of January 3 it is estimated that the following quantities of grain have

been dried on farms: Saskatchewan 16.9 million bushels, Alberta 12.9 million bushels, Manitoba 12.3 million bushels.
The answer to the second part of the question is as follows: November 372,000 bushels, December 1,042,000 bushels, January 833,000 bushels up to January 17.
